id: pm-gh1710
title: "GH-1710: budget compaction clips next_cursor to 240 characters, so --after rejects the cursor the page emitted and the rest of the result set is unreachable"
description: "GH-1710 (filed 2026-11-12). When pm list compacts its output to fit an output budget, it shortens next_cursor like any other long string: the cursor is cut to 240 characters plus an ellipsis while the page still says has_more true, so --after rejects it with invalid_query_cursor and the rest of the result set is unreachable. Reproduced on main 145286488: eight items with 180-character ids and 2,000-character titles, pm list --json --output-budget 2000 --limit 4 (with or without --for triage) emits a 241-character cursor ending in an ellipsis instead of the 351-character one. Root cause: both string-compaction walkers, compactStrings in src/sdk/read-output-budget.ts and compactContextIntentValue in src/sdk/context-intent-contracts.ts, shorten every string longer than 240 characters, and the producer cursor is rebased only when rows are dropped, so a string-only compaction keeps the clipped value. Fix: a continuation token (key cursor or ending in _cursor) is never shortened in either walker, and a cursor argument carrying an ellipsis is refused with invalid_query_cursor reason cursor_compacted (read_output_cursor_invalid for --output-cursor) naming the larger-budget read that returns it whole."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: agent-ux,"gh:1710",output-budget,pagination,read-output
created_at: "2026-11-12T21:09:08.534Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-13T03:58:20.775Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-12T23:24:17.749Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-12T23:24:17.749Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: "A budgeted list page emits next_cursor whole in JSON and TOON and with or without --for, and --after with it returns the next rows; Every continuation token in budgeted output (cursor, next_cursor, output_cursor, source_cursor) is exempt from string compaction; A cursor argument shortened by compaction is refused with invalid_query_cursor naming the larger-budget read that returns it whole"
parent: pm-5t33or
risk: medium
confidence: high
severity: high
resolution: "Both string-compaction walkers skip strings under continuation-token keys (cursor or any key ending in _cursor), so a budgeted page emits next_cursor, output_cursor and nested cursors whole in JSON and TOON, with or without --for. A cursor argument carrying an ellipsis is refused with invalid_query_cursor or read_output_cursor_invalid, reason cursor_compacted, naming the larger-budget read that returns the whole cursor."
expected_result: next_cursor is never compacted and resumes the query
actual_result: "Issue reproduction on the built CLI: page 1 emits the whole 351-character cursor and page 2 returns the next four distinct items, with and without --for triage; a hand-truncated cursor gets the cursor_compacted advice; continuation-tokens and cursor-recovery specs pass and fail against the previous walkers"
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
  pm-n98pir,related,"2026-11-12T21:09:08.534Z","harness:claude-code","cli:create:dep",detected
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-13T03:58:20.775Z","harness:claude-code","PR 1717 CI, SDK mutation gate (src/sdk/pagination.ts is in its declared scope): the cursor_compacted refusal was covered only by a spec outside the mutation test set, so its mutants reported NoCoverage and the guard survived, and the insertion shifted four existing equivalent-mutant waivers whose identities hash the mutant location. tests/unit/sdk/pagination.spec.ts now pins the refusal on both cursor flags (exact message, reason, required text and next steps), the four waivers are re-keyed to their new identities and lines with unchanged reasons, and the score floor ratchets from 98.011 to 98.072 as the gate requires.\n"
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-12T21:55:15.824Z","harness:claude-code","Implementation (2026-11-12). Both string-compaction walkers (compactStrings in src/sdk/read-output-budget.ts and compactContextIntentValue in src/sdk/context-intent-contracts.ts) now skip any string under a continuation-token key, decided by isContinuationTokenKey in src/core/shared/text-normalization.ts: the key cursor or any key ending in _cursor (next_cursor, output_cursor, source_cursor, base_source_cursor). A non-string value under such a key is still walked, so explanatory text nested under a cursor object keeps compacting. The cursor decoders refuse an argument carrying an ellipsis before parsing: decodeQueryCursorEnvelope (--after and --cursor) with invalid_query_cursor and reason cursor_compacted, decodeReadOutputContinuationCursor (--output-cursor) with read_output_cursor_invalid and the same reason; both name the larger-budget read that returns the whole cursor. Cursor lengths stay bounded by MAX_CURSOR_LENGTH, so exempting them cannot defeat the budget. Verified on the built CLI with the issue reproduction: page 1 emits the whole 351-character cursor and page 2 returns the next four items, with and without --for triage."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-12T23:24:10.485Z","harness:claude-code","When an output transform shortens strings to fit a budget, list which strings are machine input for the next call (cursors, tokens, replay commands) and exempt them by key, in every walker that applies the transform. A rebase-on-row-drop step hides the defect whenever rows are dropped, so the failing case is a string-only compaction."
